<XDFFORMAT version="1.80">
  <XDFHEADER>
    <flags>0x1</flags>
    <fileversion>BMS46-Q28G-v1.09-STABLE-GALLETTO32</fileversion>
    <deftitle>BMS46 Q28G v1.09 STABLE - FULL-DERIVED GALLETTO 32KB</deftitle>
    <description>Reverse-engineered full-read XDF for exact BMS46 01119700F000Q28G / BMW DME 1430940, 262144-byte firmware image. Direct-reference, single-xref, pointer/literal, structured-vector/bitfield and indirect/address-register coverage audits are closed. TunerPro read/write round-trip was validated across 8-bit, signed 8-bit, Motorola 16-bit, signed 16-bit, bitmask and map-cell edits. Native BMS46 CRC16/ARC validation is included as a companion tool. Display names are cleaned for tuner use; original audit names are preserved in V100_TITLE_MAPPING.csv. Exact Bosch/DAMOS symbol names cannot be guaranteed where the binary contains no OEM symbols; such items remain documented as code-derived or expert/internal rather than guessed. v1.01 addendum: VMax speed threshold and hysteresis physical scale are code-confirmed as 1 raw count = 1 km/h. v1.09: TunerPro opening confirmed with the Lambda2 controls and all 76 DTC catalog entries; definitions remain calibration-neutral until edited by the user.

[GALLETTO32 DERIVATIVE] Calibration-only derivative for the 32KB Galletto layout supplied by the user. The supplied PARTIAL/Galletto XDF pair shows the Galletto map locations rebased by 0x8010 for the common calibration maps. All retained stable-full definitions are therefore rebased by -0x8010. Program/boot/UIF items outside the 32KB calibration image are intentionally omitted.</description>
    <author>BMS46 Q28G reproducible reverse-engineering project</author>
    <BASEOFFSET offset="0" subtract="0" />
    <DEFAULTS datasizeinbits="8" sigdigits="4" outputtype="1" signed="0" lsbfirst="0" float="0" />
    <REGION type="0xFFFFFFFF" startaddress="0x0" size="0x8000" regioncolor="0x0" regionflags="0x0" name="Q28G Galletto 32KB calibration" desc="32KB Galletto calibration layout; full Q28G addresses rebased by -0x8010." />
