  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6241" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>ICV Low Voltage RPM Target</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.51 CODE-DERIVED] In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_016452, the low-voltage idle state is entered when Engine_Alternator is below 0x889B under the required idle/stationary conditions. While that state bit is active, 0x8898 is shifted left by 6 and supplied as the target to the state slew function for FF8438. Because FF8338/64 is RPM/10 in the same logic, this byte is a 10-RPM-per-bit target. Q28G raw 84 -&gt; 840 RPM.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x888" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>RPM</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <rangehigh>2550</rangehigh>
    <rangelow>0</rangelow>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X * 10">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6242" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>ICV Cold Ambient Minimum RPM Clamp</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.51 CODE-DERIVED] PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_016452 sets a cold-ambient state bit from Vehicle_Ambient_Temp using 0x8B48/0x8B49. When that state bit is active, the selected idle RPM byte is compared with 0x8899 and raised to 0x8899 if lower; the result is then shifted left by 6 into the FF8338 RPM-word domain. This gives 10 RPM per byte count. Q28G raw 60 -&gt; 600 RPM.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x889" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>RPM</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <rangehigh>2550</rangehigh>
    <rangelow>0</rangelow>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X * 10">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6243" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>ICV Low Voltage Entry Threshold</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.51 CODE-DERIVED] PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_016452 compares Engine_Alternator FF832A directly with 0x889B and enters the low-voltage idle state when voltage is below this threshold under the required idle/stationary conditions. The existing ICV_Correction_Voltage and injector-voltage axes establish 0.094 V/bit for FF832A. Q28G raw 131 -&gt; 12.314 V. Adjacent 0x889C is the exit hysteresis and is reserved for the later exhaustiveness pass because it has only one direct xref.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x88B" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>V</units>
    <decimalpl>3</decimalpl>
    <rangehigh>23.97</rangehigh>
    <rangelow>0</rangelow>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X * 0.094">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6244" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>ICV Low Voltage Reentry Holdoff</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.51 CODE-DERIVED] 0x889D initializes FF8433 during idle initialization and again when PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_016452 leaves the low-voltage idle state. While FF8433 is nonzero the state-entry path decrements it instead of re-entering the state. Q28G raw 44. This is therefore a re-entry holdoff/countdown in controller update cycles; no wall-clock conversion is asserted.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x88D" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
