    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X * 0.75 - 48">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6246" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>DFCO Restore Fuel Ignition Corrections Enable</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.52 CODE-DERIVED] set_Engine_Timing_Advance tests 0x85C9 and, when enabled with FF84E5 bit0 set, restores the saved ignition target FF84F2 then clears the restore-state bit. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01C346 the same 0x85C9 enables application of FF84E8, the DFCO restore fuel factor, to the fuel calculation. Q28G raw=1. This is therefore a shared DFCO/deceleration restore-correction enable for fuel and ignition; it is not a generic feature switch.</description>
