  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x6249" vislevel="1" flags="0xC">
    <title>Lambda Additive Trim RPM Normalization Gain</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.52 CODE-DERIVED] handler_Emission_System forms the additive lambda-trim word written to FF8514 by taking either the learned trim word FF97F2 or alternate trim source FF8530, centering it around 0x8000, multiplying by 0x92C2, dividing by Engine_RPM FF8334, and applying the path-specific fixed shift. Q28G raw=25. The mechanical role as the RPM-normalization gain is direct; no unsupported physical-unit conversion is asserted.</description>
