    <title>ASC Internal Ramp Output Upper Clamp</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.52 CODE-DERIVED] In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_02A5FE, when ASC state FF890F equals 1, current byte FF88F0 is compared directly with 0x9A0A; values at or above the calibration are replaced by 0x9A0A. Q28G raw=38. This is an explicit upper clamp in the ASC internal ramp/output domain.</description>
