  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEF03" flags="0x0">
    <title>Misfire Channel Scaling Correction Vector Q14</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 STRUCTURED VECTOR / CODE-DERIVED / EXPERT] Four signed bytes at 0x831C..0x831F are indexed through the runtime channel permutation table 0x14AAC = [0,2,3,1] in the misfire path. Each selected byte is sign-extended, multiplied by the current internal word and shifted right 14, then added back to that word. Thus each element is a signed Q14 fractional correction. Q28G stock is 0,0,0,0. This is diagnostic/misfire processing, not normal engine tuning.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="11" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>vector index</units>
      <indexcount>4</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <outputtype>4</outputtype>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="Vector 0" />
      <LABEL index="1" value="Vector 1" />
      <LABEL index="2" value="Vector 2" />
      <LABEL index="3" value="Vector 3" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <indexcount>1</indexcount>
      <outputtype>4</outputtype>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="z">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x01" mmedaddress="0x30C" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedrowcount="1" mmedcolcount="4" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>% correction</units>
      <decimalpl>6</decimalpl>
      <min>-0.78125</min>
      <max>0.775147</max>
      <outputtype>1</outputtype>
      <MATH equation="X * 100 / 16384">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
  </XDFTABLE>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xEF04">
    <title>Lambda State LowBand Transition Disable</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 MASK-PRESERVING FLAG / CODE-DERIVED] Bit0 of calibration byte 0x92C3. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01DF34, when this bit is SET the low-band lambda-state transition that would set runtime bit1 is inhibited. Stock 0x92C3=0xFC, so bit0 is CLEAR and the transition is permitted. TunerPro flag editing changes only mask 0x01 and preserves bits1..7.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="6" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x12B3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xEF05">
    <title>Lambda State HighBand Transition Disable</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 MASK-PRESERVING FLAG / CODE-DERIVED] Bit1 of calibration byte 0x92C3. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01DF34, when this bit is SET the high-band lambda-state transition that would set runtime bit2 is inhibited. Stock 0x92C3=0xFC, so bit1 is CLEAR and the transition is permitted. TunerPro flag editing changes only mask 0x02 and preserves bits0 and2..7.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="6" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x12B3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x02</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEF06" flags="0x0">
    <title>Ignition Per Cylinder Static Offset Vector</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 STRUCTURED VECTOR / CODE-DERIVED / EXPERT] Four bytes at 0xA9AA..0xA9AD are consumed by set_Engine_Timing_Advance once per cylinder/channel. The routine walks the vector in reverse (A9AD down to A9AA), adds the byte to the encoded ignition value, then subtracts 0x80 before applying the normal ignition clamps. Therefore 0x80 is zero correction and one raw count equals 0.75 crank degree. Q28G stock is 0x80,0x80,0x80,0x80 = 0 deg correction. The exact physical cylinder-to-storage-index naming is not asserted; preserve stock unless channel mapping is independently verified.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>stored vector index</units>
      <indexcount>4</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <outputtype>4</outputtype>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="Stored 0" />
      <LABEL index="1" value="Stored 1" />
      <LABEL index="2" value="Stored 2" />
      <LABEL index="3" value="Stored 3" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <indexcount>1</indexcount>
      <outputtype>4</outputtype>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="z">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x299A" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedrowcount="1" mmedcolcount="4" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>deg correction</units>
      <decimalpl>2</decimalpl>
      <min>-96</min>
      <max>95.25</max>
      <outputtype>1</outputtype>
      <MATH equation="(X - 128) * 0.75">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
  </XDFTABLE>
  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEF07" flags="0x0">
    <title>Knock RPM State Band Boundaries</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 STRUCTURED VECTOR / CODE-DERIVED / INFERRED] Shared six-byte RPM-boundary vector at 0x9E06..0x9E0B used by calculate_Engine_Knock. The 0x9E06 view indexes elements 0..4 using the current low-nibble knock state and applies 0x9DF0 RPM hysteresis on the opposite transition. The 0x9E07 view scans elements 1..5 to classify the next RPM band. Values are in the established Engine_RPM byte domain of 40 RPM/count. Q28G stock = 480,1440,2400,4040,5400,10200 RPM.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="8" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>boundary</units>
      <indexcount>6</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <outputtype>4</outputtype>
